<title>USA: Airport Systems says wins Thailand orders.</title>
<headline>Airport Systems says wins Thailand orders.</headline>
<dateline>OVERLAND PARK, Kan. 1996-09-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Airport Systems International said it won contracts valued at $2.4 million for navigational and landing aid systems in Thailand.</p>
<p>The company expects to ship the equipment during its second fiscal quarter ending in October, it said.</p>
<p>Airport Systems said it will provide Thailand with eight systems, each consisting of a Model 1150 VHF Omni-Range and Model 1119 Distance Measuring Equipment.</p>
<p>Airport Systems will also provide the training related to the ongoing operation of these systems, it said.</p>
<p>--Chicago Newsdesk 312-408-8787</p>
</text>
